Tue Nov 17 11:00:00 UTC 2026 - Eyad Issa <eyadlorenzo@gmail.com>

- Update to version 1.3.0:
  * Add address space support and overlap checks.
  * Improve static hwloc build options and installation.
- Changes in version 1.2.0:
  * Add cache line size queries to memory providers.
  * Improve Level Zero host allocations and hwloc builds.
  * Fix memory leaks, cleanup failures and potential memory
    corruption.
- Changes in version 1.1.0:
  * Add memory properties, pool trimming and Level Zero eviction
    APIs.
  * Extend CTL and add names to pools and providers.
  * Remove the deprecated UMF_DISABLE_HWLOC option.
  * Fix pool and provider errors and hwloc initialization.
- Changes in version 1.0.3:
  * Load libcuda.so.1 instead of libcuda.so on Linux.
- Changes in version 1.0.2:
  * Initialize hwloc topology only before the first fork.
- Changes in version 1.0.1:
  * Improve topology initialization and fix the jemalloc Ninja
    build.
  * Check whether providers support split operations.
- Changes in version 1.0.0:
  * Introduce an experimental CTL API and umfPoolGetName.
  * Improve jemalloc pool arenas and make umfInit thread-safe.
  * Change the public API and shared library ABI; introduce a
    backward compatibility guarantee for the stable API.
- Changes in version 0.11.2:
  * Retrieve NUMA nodes by OS index instead of logical index.
- Changes in version 0.11.1:
  * Check global state destruction in destructors and adjust
    logging.
- Rename the runtime package to libumf1 to match the new SONAME.
- Recommend libtbbmalloc2 for the scalable pool and proxy library.
- Correct the license to include the LLVM exception.

